obtained from differences, for example. We thus obtain \(y_{1}(x_{0}\pm H)\) and \(y_{2}(x_{0}\pm H)\).

Now suppose

\[W^{\prime}(a,\,x_{0})=W^{\prime*}(a,\,x_{0})+\lambda\]

then, for all \(x\)

\[W(a,\,x)=y_{1}(x)+\lambda y_{2}(x)\]

and in particular

\[W(a,\,x_{0}\pm H)=y_{1}(x_{0}\pm H)+\lambda y_{2}(x_{0}\pm H)\]

The values of \(W(a,\,x_{0}\pm H)\) may be read from the tables and two independent estimates of \(\lambda\) obtained, whence

\[W^{\prime}(a,\,x_{0})=W^{\prime*}(a,\,x_{0})+\lambda\]

to a suitable accuracy.

